<%--
_Sys_Task_Console - one _tasks row's log in an xterm.js terminal, following the task live.

$task_id - the _tasks id (required)

Every line the task writes to its log appears as it is written: $task->info() / error() /
debug() / update_progress(), and anything the task prints (echo, print, var_dump), which a
pool worker records as `output` lines. The status line under the terminal is the row's
status, the line count and, while running, the last heartbeat.

Live updates ride Task_Changed_Topic and need realtime (REALTIME_ENABLED); without it the
console shows the log as it was when the page opened, and Refresh reads what is new.

Events OUT: 'status_changed' {status}.
--%>
<Define:_Sys_Task_Console tag="div">
    <div class="_Sys_Task_Console__screen" $sid="screen"></div>
    <div class="_Sys_Task_Console__bar">
        <span class="_Sys_Task_Console__status" $sid="status"></span>
        <% if (this.state.live) { %>
            <span class="_Sys_Task_Console__live"><i class="bi bi-broadcast"></i> live</span>
        <% } else { %>
            <span class="_Sys_Task_Console__live">live updates off (realtime is disabled)</span>
        <% } %>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-secondary" data-action="refresh">
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-clockwise"></i> Refresh
        </button>
    </div>
</Define:_Sys_Task_Console>
